  "limitations": [
    "This concerns EPFO staff appraisal (APAR) and vigilance clearance, not EPF member services. Cadre, level and the officer's own position must be checked in the circular and its annexures.",
    "Each revised-timeline circular lists maximum dates for the stated activities; later circulars revise earlier dates. As of a given date, the most recent circular issued on or before it states the operative timeline for the activities it lists; this history does not compute deadlines or auto-forward dates.",
    "The 26 Aug 2025 and 20 Apr 2026 circulars are 87-page files that include a SPARROW user manual; only the circular pages and the timeline tables are relied on.",
    "The 22 Sep 2025 circular moves MTS, electrician, lift operator, driver and similar cadres to the EPFO HR Portal for 2024-25. The 20 Apr 2026 circular excludes those cadres from SPARROW for 2025-26.",
    "No commencement date is stated, so issue date is not treated as commencement. Missing or unread earlier circulars (for example the 2014 office order and 2015 and April 2017 vigilance letters cited in the checked documents, and the March 2021 HR-Soft circular) are not in this collection.",
    "APAR cycles before 2020-21 and between 2021-22 and 2023-24, individual vigilance clearance requests (for example on superannuation) and DoPT rules are not covered.",
    "Header dates on some scans are partly illegible. Issue dates follow the issuer listing and agree with the dates cited in later circulars of the same chain. The issuer table lists one 25 March 2026 circular twice (also as 25 March 2025); 25 March 2026 is correct.",
    "PDFs were read from the issuer mirror on 3 November 2026 because the public site returned 404 for these paths that day; recorded SHA-256 values apply to those files. Scanned pages are OCR."
  ]
